   "id": "wages-000",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Wages and Housing Affordability: Person 2\n",
    "**Datathon for Social Good 2026 · Bay Area Affordability Project**\n",
    "\n",
    "Estimates advertised annual pay for 12 featured jobs, adds historical\n",
    "BLS wage-growth scenarios, and compares wages with ZIP-level housing costs.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main outputs:** `wages_by_job_city.csv` and `burden_by_job_zip.csv`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run instructions:** Edit the paths below, upload the housing CSV and\n",
    "five BLS Excel files, then run the notebook from top to bottom.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pending checks:** Independently verify the mortgage rate and review\n",
    "BLS metro boundaries. Wage projections are scenarios, not validated forecasts.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "wages-001",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Connect Drive and configure paths\n",
    "\n",
    "The full Indeed file is on Drive. Housing and BLS files are uploaded to `/content`. Uploaded files disappear when the runtime resets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "wages-002",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "full_path = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/Copy of indeed_job_listings.csv\"\n",
    "output_dir = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/affordability_outputs\")\n",
    "output_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "required = [Path(full_path), Path(\"/content/albert_housing_by_zip.csv\")]\n",
    "required += [Path(f\"/content/MSA_M{y}_dl.xlsx\") for y in range(2021, 2026)]\n",
    "missing = [str(p) for p in required if not p.exists()]\n",
    "if missing:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Upload or configure: \" + \", \".join(missing))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "wages-003",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Define job matching and salary conversion\n",
    "\n",
    "Match titles to one featured job. Salary ranges use their midpoint. Hourly × 2,080; weekly × 52; monthly × 12. One-sided bounds, unsupported units, and annual equivalents outside $15,000–$1,000,000 remain missing. Tips are excluded. Annualization assumes full-time work."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "wages-004",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "# Starting rules; review matches before using them for final results\n",
    "job_rules = {\n",
    "    \"Cashier\": r\"\\bcashier\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Retail sales\": r\"\\bretail sales\\b|\\bsales associate\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Food service worker\": r\"\\bfood service worker\\b|\\bbarista\\b|\\bserver\\b|\\bhost person\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Home health aide\": r\"\\bhome health aide\\b|\\bpersonal care aide\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Childcare worker\": r\"\\bchildcare\\b|\\bchild care\\b|\\bdaycare\\b|\\bnanny\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Warehouse worker\": r\"\\bwarehouse\\b|\\bmaterial handler\\b|\\border picker\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Medical assistant\": r\"\\bmedical assistant\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Teacher\": r\"\\bteacher\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Registered nurse\": r\"\\bregistered nurse\\b|\\brn\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Electrician\": r\"\\belectrician\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Accountant\": r\"\\baccountant\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Software engineer\": r\"\\bsoftware engineer\\b|\\bsoftware developer\\b\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "def match_job(title):\n",
    "    title = str(title).lower()\n",
    "    matches = [\n",
    "        job for job, pattern in job_rules.items()\n",
    "        if re.search(pattern, title)\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    return matches[0] if len(matches) == 1 else pd.NA\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def annualize_salary(value):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(value):\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "    text = str(value).lower().replace(\",\", \"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Keep one-sided bounds separate rather than treating them as exact pay\n",
    "    if re.search(r\"\\bfrom\\b|\\bup to\\b|\\bdesde\\b|\\bhasta\\b\", text):\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "    amounts = re.findall(r\"\\$\\s*(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*([kK]?)\", text)\n",
    "    if not amounts or len(amounts) > 2:\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "    numbers = [\n",
    "        float(number) * (1000 if suffix else 1)\n",
    "        for number, suffix in amounts\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    pay = sum(numbers) / len(numbers)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if re.search(r\"\\bhour\\b|\\bhora\\b\", text):\n",
    "        pay *= 2080\n",
    "    elif re.search(r\"\\bmonth\\b|\\bmes\\b\", text):\n",
    "        pay *= 12\n",
    "    elif re.search(r\"\\bweek\\b|\\bsemana\\b\", text):\n",
    "        pay *= 52\n",
    "    elif not re.search(r\"\\byear\\b|\\bannual\\b|\\baño\\b\", text):\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "    return pay if 15000 <= pay <= 1000000 else np.nan\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "wages-005",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Read and deduplicate the full Indeed dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "Read in 100,000-row chunks and keep featured jobs. Remove duplicates on title, company, and location. Extract explicit California cities."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "wages-006",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Uses match_job() from your earlier cell\n",
    "columns = [\n",
    "    \"jobid\", \"job_title\", \"company_name\", \"location\",\n",
    "    \"job_location\", \"region\", \"salary_formatted\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "parts = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, chunk in enumerate(\n",
    "    pd.read_csv(\n",
    "        full_path,\n",
    "        usecols=columns,\n",
    "        dtype=\"string\",\n",
    "        chunksize=100_000\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    start=1\n",
    "):\n",
    "    chunk[\"job\"] = chunk[\"job_title\"].apply(match_job)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Keep featured jobs\n",
    "    keep = chunk.loc[chunk[\"job\"].notna()].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Exclude nurse management roles\n",
    "    nurse_manager = (\n",
    "        keep[\"job\"].eq(\"Registered nurse\")\n",
    "        & keep[\"job_title\"].str.contains(\n",
    "            r\"\\bmanager\\b|\\bdirector\\b|\\bsupervisor\\b\",\n",
    "            case=False, na=False\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    keep = keep.loc[~nurse_manager]\n",
    "\n",
    "    parts.append(keep)\n",
    "    print(f\"Chunk {i}: kept {len(keep):,} postings\")\n",
    "\n",
    "full_jobs = pd.concat(parts, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "full_jobs = full_jobs.drop_duplicates(\n",
    "    subset=[\"job_title\", \"company_name\", \"location\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Extract California cities, including those after street addresses\n",
    "full_jobs[\"city\"] = full_jobs[\"location\"].str.extract(\n",
    "    r\"(?:^|,)\\s*([^,]+),\\s*CA(?:\\s+\\d{5}(?:-\\d{4})?)?\\s*$\",\n",
    "    expand=False\n",
    ").str.strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTotal featured-job postings: {len(full_jobs):,}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nCalifornia cities found:\")\n",
    "print(full_jobs[\"city\"].value_counts().to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "wages-007",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Filter to Bay Area cities and communities\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the documented city-to-county lookup. It covers names observed in the original file; review unmatched cities if the input changes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "wages-008",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bay Area cities/communities appearing in your full-file results\n",
    "places_by_county = {\n",
    "    \"Alameda\": \"\"\"Alameda|Albany|Berkeley|Castro Valley|Dublin|\n",
    "Emeryville|Fremont|Hayward|Livermore|Newark|Oakland|Pleasanton|\n",
    "San Leandro|San Lorenzo|Union City|Coast Guard Island\"\"\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"Contra Costa\": \"\"\"Alamo|Antioch|Bay Point|Brentwood|Clayton|\n",
    "Concord|Danville|Discovery Bay|El Cerrito|El Sobrante|Hercules|\n",
    "Lafayette|Martinez|Moraga|North Richmond|Oakley|Orinda|Pinole|\n",
    "Pittsburg|Pleasant Hill|Richmond|Rodeo|San Pablo|San Ramon|\n",
    "Walnut Creek\"\"\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"Marin\": \"\"\"Corte Madera|Fairfax|Greenbrae|Kentfield|Larkspur|\n",
    "Marin City|Marshall|Mill Valley|Novato|San Anselmo|San Rafael|\n",
    "Sausalito|Tiburon\"\"\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"Napa\": \"\"\"American Canyon|Angwin|Calistoga|Napa|Rutherford|\n",
    "Saint Helena|Yountville\"\"\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"San Francisco\": \"San Francisco\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"San Mateo\": \"\"\"Atherton|Belmont|Brisbane|Burlingame|Colma|\n",
    "Daly City|East Palo Alto|Foster City|Half Moon Bay|Hillsborough|\n",
    "Menlo Park|Millbrae|Pacifica|Redwood City|San Bruno|San Carlos|\n",
    "San Mateo|South San Francisco|West Menlo Park|Woodside\"\"\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"Santa Clara\": \"\"\"Alviso|Campbell|Cupertino|Gilroy|Los Altos|\n",
    "Los Gatos|Milpitas|Moffett Field|Morgan Hill|Mountain View|\n",
    "Palo Alto|San Jose|San Martin|Santa Clara|Saratoga|Stanford|\n",
    "Sunnyvale\"\"\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"Solano\": \"\"\"Benicia|Dixon|Fairfield|Rio Vista|Suisun City|\n",
    "Travis AFB|Vacaville|Vallejo\"\"\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"Sonoma\": \"\"\"Bodega Bay|Cloverdale|Cotati|Forestville|\n",
    "Guerneville|Healdsburg|Occidental|Penngrove|Petaluma|\n",
    "Rohnert Park|Santa Rosa|Sebastopol|Sonoma|Windsor\"\"\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "city_to_county = {\n",
    "    place.strip(): county\n",
    "    for county, places in places_by_county.items()\n",
    "    for place in places.split(\"|\")\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "full_jobs[\"county\"] = full_jobs[\"city\"].map(city_to_county)\n",
    "bay_full = full_jobs.loc[full_jobs[\"county\"].notna()].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Bay Area featured-job postings:\", len(bay_full))\n",
    "print(\"\\nPostings per job:\")\n",
    "print(bay_full[\"job\"].value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nPostings per county:\")\n",
    "print(bay_full[\"county\"].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "wages-009",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Convert salaries and inspect title matches\n",
    "\n",
    "Missing salary text differs from listed pay that cannot be converted. Review up to 20 postings per job using a fixed random seed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "wages-010",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Apply the salary conversion function from your earlier cell\n",
    "bay_full[\"annual_pay\"] = bay_full[\"salary_formatted\"].apply(\n",
    "    annualize_salary\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Missing salary is different from a listed salary we couldn't convert\n",
    "bay_full[\"pay_missing\"] = (\n",
    "    bay_full[\"salary_formatted\"].fillna(\"\").str.strip().eq(\"\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "wages_full = (\n",
    "    bay_full.groupby([\"job\", \"city\"], as_index=False)\n",
    "    .agg(\n",
    "        median_pay=(\"annual_pay\", \"median\"),\n",
    "        n_postings=(\"job_title\", \"size\"),\n",
    "        n_usable_pay=(\"annual_pay\", \"count\"),\n",
    "        share_missing_pay=(\"pay_missing\", \"mean\")\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "wages_full[\"median_pay\"] = wages_full[\"median_pay\"].round(2)\n",
    "wages_full[\"thin_data\"] = wages_full[\"n_postings\"] < 10\n",
    "\n",
    "display(wages_full.head(20))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Job/city groups:\", len(wages_full))\n",
    "print(\"Postings with usable pay:\", bay_full[\"annual_pay\"].notna().sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Inspect listed salaries that weren't converted\n",
    "needs_review = bay_full.loc[\n",
    "    ~bay_full[\"pay_missing\"] & bay_full[\"annual_pay\"].isna(),\n",
    "    [\"job\", \"salary_formatted\"]\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nListed salaries needing review:\")\n",
    "display(needs_review.drop_duplicates().head(25))\n",
    "# Sample up to 20 postings per job for manual review\n",
    "review = pd.concat(\n",
    "    [\n",
    "        group.sample(n=min(20, len(group)), random_state=42)\n",
    "        for _, group in bay_full.groupby(\"job\")\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    ignore_index=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display every sampled title without truncating it\n",
    "with pd.option_context(\n",
    "    \"display.max_rows\", 250,\n",
    "    \"display.max_colwidth\", None\n",
    "):\n",
    "    display(\n",
    "        review[[\"job\", \"job_title\", \"city\"]]\n",
    "        .sort_values([\"job\", \"job_title\"])\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "wages-011",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Apply reviewed occupation exclusions\n",
    "\n",
    "Exclude pet daycare, computing-server roles, investment sales, instructors, nurse specialists, warehouse management, and internships."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "wages-012",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Rules based on the manual title review\n",
    "exclusions = {\n",
    "    \"Childcare worker\": r\"\\bdog\\b|\\bpet\\b|\\bpayment analyst\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Food service worker\": (\n",
    "        r\"\\bengineer\\b|\\bsoftware\\b|\\bplatform\\b|\\bsystems?\\b\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"Home health aide\": r\"\\binstructor\\b|\\bteacher\\b|\\btrainer\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Retail sales\": (\n",
    "        r\"\\bprivate equity\\b|\\binvestment\\b|\\binside sales\\b\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"Registered nurse\": (\n",
    "        r\"\\banesthetist\\b|\\bpractitioner\\b|\\bcrna\\b|\"\n",
    "        r\"\\bmanager\\b|\\bdirector\\b|\\bsupervisor\\b\"\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    \"Warehouse worker\": r\"\\bmanager\\b|\\bsupervisor\\b|\\bdirector\\b\",\n",
    "    \"Software engineer\": r\"\\bintern\\b|\\binternship\\b\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Start from bay_full so rerunning this cell is safe\n",
    "bay_reviewed = bay_full.copy()\n",
    "remove = pd.Series(False, index=bay_reviewed.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "for job, pattern in exclusions.items():\n",
    "    remove |= (\n",
    "        bay_reviewed[\"job\"].eq(job)\n",
    "        & bay_reviewed[\"job_title\"].str.contains(\n",
    "            pattern, case=False, na=False, regex=True\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Excluded postings:\", remove.sum())\n",
    "bay_reviewed = bay_reviewed.loc[~remove].copy()\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "wages-013",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Narrow teachers to K–12\n",
    "\n",
    "Require explicit school-level evidence. Exclude preschool, assistants, substitutes, tutoring, after-school, and identified special education."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "wages-014",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "titles = bay_reviewed[\"job_title\"].fillna(\"\")\n",
    "is_teacher = bay_reviewed[\"job\"].eq(\"Teacher\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Explicit evidence of a K–12 school level\n",
    "k12 = titles.str.contains(\n",
    "    r\"elementary|middle school|high school|\"\n",
    "    r\"lower school|upper school|secondary|\"\n",
    "    r\"kindergarten|\\bTK\\b|homeroom|\"\n",
    "    r\"\\bK[\\s–-]*(?:12|8|5)\\b|\"\n",
    "    r\"\\b(?:[1-9]|1[0-2])(?:st|nd|rd|th)?\\s*grade\",\n",
    "    case=False, regex=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep classroom teachers separate from these roles\n",
    "exclude = titles.str.contains(\n",
    "    r\"preschool|pre-school|pre-k\\b|infant|toddler|\"\n",
    "    r\"early childhood|assistant|associate|aide|\"\n",
    "    r\"substitute|\\bsub\\b|after[\\s-]?school|\"\n",
    "    r\"special education|\\bSPED\\b|education specialist|\"\n",
    "    r\"AI trainer|tutor\",\n",
    "    case=False, regex=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "keep_teacher = k12 & ~exclude\n",
    "\n",
    "bay_final = bay_reviewed.loc[\n",
    "    ~is_teacher | keep_teacher\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "bay_final.loc[\n",
    "    bay_final[\"job\"].eq(\"Teacher\"), \"job\"\n",
    "] = \"K–12 teacher\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Preserve excluded/ambiguous teacher titles for review\n",
    "teacher_review = bay_reviewed.loc[\n",
    "    is_teacher & ~keep_teacher\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"K–12 teacher postings retained:\", keep_teacher[is_teacher].sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "display(\n",
    "    bay_final.loc[\n",
    "        bay_final[\"job\"].eq(\"K–12 teacher\"),\n",
    "        [\"job_title\", \"city\", \"annual_pay\"]\n",
    "    ].sort_values(\"job_title\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "# Exclude the additional special-education abbreviation\n",
    "remove = (\n",
    "    bay_final[\"job\"].eq(\"K–12 teacher\")\n",
    "    & bay_final[\"job_title\"].str.contains(\n",
    "        r\"\\bsp[\\s.-]*ed\\b\",\n",
    "        case=False, na=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "bay_final = bay_final.loc[~remove].copy()\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "wages-015",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Summarize pay by job and city\n",
    "\n",
    "`thin_data` flags fewer than 10 postings. `thin_pay_data` flags fewer than 10 usable salaries. Unavailable medians remain blank."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "wages-016",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "wages_full = (\n",
    "    bay_final.groupby([\"job\", \"city\"], as_index=False)\n",
    "    .agg(\n",
    "        median_pay=(\"annual_pay\", \"median\"),\n",
    "        n_postings=(\"job_title\", \"size\"),\n",
    "        n_usable_pay=(\"annual_pay\", \"count\"),\n",
    "        share_missing_pay=(\"pay_missing\", \"mean\")\n",
